meta {
  name: Get Current User
  type: http
  seq: 5
  tags: [
    auth
    protected
  ]
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Returns the public user and userDetails profiles for the access token subject. userDetails is null when the user has not created a details row.

  Run Login first so Bruno captures `accessToken` as a runtime variable. You can also set `accessToken` manually in the active environment for an existing token.

  Success response: 200 with data.user and data.userDetails in camelCase; data.user.isEmailVerified is true for an authenticated account. The response never includes a password or password hash.
  Error response: 401 `UNAUTHORIZED` when the token is missing, malformed, invalid, expired, or belongs to a soft-deleted user; pending accounts receive 403 `EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED`.
}
